I thought this was worthy of public notice:
=C2=A0
=C2=A0
=C2=A0
Unfortunately, we removed 16-bit support from the ACPICA code (and thus Acp=
iExec) years ago, as it was felt that 16-bit code (and DOS) was permanently=
 gone. The original code is still in our source tree, but it is obviously v=
ery, very downreved.
=C2=A0
Bob
=C2=A0
=C2=A0
15 December 2006. Summary of changes for version 20061215:
=C2=A0
1) ACPI CA Core Subsystem:
=C2=A0
Support for 16-bit ACPICA has been completely removed since it is no =

longer necessary and it clutters the code. All 16-bit macros, types, and =

conditional compiles have been removed, cleaning up and simplifying the =

code across the entire subsystem. DOS support is no longer needed since the =

bootable Linux firmware kit is now available.
=C2=A0
=C2=A0
=C2=A0
=C2=A0
